{"id": "20479765", "revid": "44417386", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20479765", "title": "National Highway 77 (India, old numbering)", "text": "National Highway 77 is a National Highway of India entirely within the state of Bihar that links Hajipur to Sonbarsa near India-Nepal border, and is long. In 2010, the highway was renumbered to form part of present-day NH 22.\nSee also.\nThe national highway has very important from commercial Point view as it connects North Bihar with South Bihar. It also important because it directly connects south Bihar with the International Border of Nepal."}
