{"id": "20480643", "revid": "1175300", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20480643", "title": "Samuel Miller House", "text": "The Samuel Miller House is a historic home located at Lynchburg, Virginia, United States. It is associated with Samuel Miller (1792-1869), a successful businessman and investor who was among the wealthiest men in the South during the years preceding the American Civil War. It is a large frame house erected between 1826 and 1829, and expanded and modified numerous times through the 20th century. Outbuildings consist of a cottage, stable, woodshed, and garage. The surrounding property was contested terrain during the siege of Lynchburg (June 1864), when a cavalry skirmish occurred on the property.\nIt was listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1992."}
{"id": "20480644", "revid": "28481209", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20480644", "title": "Weld River", "text": "The Weld River is a river in the South West region of Western Australia.\nThe river rises below Mount Burnside in the Lake Muir State forest. The river flows in a southerly direction through the Shannon National Park until it flows into the Deep River, of which it is a tributary.\nThe water quality of the river is excellent and is considered fresh."}
