{"id": "20480892", "revid": "9784415", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20480892", "title": "Herbert Franke (sinologist)", "text": "Herbert Franke (27 September 1914 \u2013 10 June 2011) was a German historian of China. He is particularly known for his works on the history of the Jurchen (Jin) and Mongol (Yuan) empires in China.\nAfter the end of World War II, Herbert Franke, along with Wolfgang Bauer, was instrumental in establishing the Sinological Section in the University of Munich. Later, he succeeded Erich Haenisch as the head of the Sinology Department at that university.\nHe is one of the authors of volume 6 of \"The Cambridge History of China\" dealing with the history of China under the Khitan, Jurchen and Mongol regimes."}
