{"id": "20483043", "revid": "41296920", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20483043", "title": "Albert \u00dcksip", "text": "Albert Aleksander \u00dcksip (8 December 1886 in Narva \u2013 10 August 1966 in Tallinn, Estonian SSR, Soviet Union) was an Estonian actor, botanist (hieraciologist) and translator. He published a part of his works in Russian as \u0410\u043b\u044c\u0431\u0435\u0440\u0442 \u042f\u043a\u043e\u0432\u043b\u0435\u0432\u0438\u0447 \u042e\u043a\u0441\u0438\u043f, so besides the correct form \u00dcksip there exist several variants of his name: Ueksip, Juxip, Juksip and \u00dcxip.\nIn 1902 he graduated from Narva city school. Between 1902 and 1923 he worked at Kreenholm Manufacturing Company. From 1923 to 1949 he was an actor of the national Estonian theatre \"Estonia\". After his retirement he worked on the genus \"Hieracium\", publishing two monographs and several smaller papers. He authored several hundred names in this difficult genus, including both new species he described and new nomenclatural combinations.\nThere exists a documentary film about him, dated from 1963."}
