{"id": "20483794", "revid": "2004589", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20483794", "title": "Crozier Channel", "text": "The Crozier Channel () is a natural waterway through the central Canadian Arctic Archipelago in the Northwest Territories of Canada. It separates Prince Patrick Island (to the north-west) and Eglinton Island (to the south-east). It opens into the McClure Strait at its southern end. It is named for the explorer, Francis Crozier; one of several such memorials in the Canadian Arctic."}
